    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1512": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Campus Security Officer Req #230 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 7, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 23, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. CAMPUS SECURITY OFFICER Cape Breton University (CBU) invites applications for the position of Campus Security Officer within the Emergency Management & Security Services department. This is a full-time continuing position . Cape Breton University (CBU) is committed to providing a safe and secure environment for employees and students to work, study, and live. CBU has established a proactive Campus Safety program aimed at education and fostering a safe environment for all. PURPOSE: Under the general supervision of the Emergency Management & Security Services Manager, the Campus Security Officer is responsible for fostering a safe, secure, and inclusive campus community through education, prevention, and the enforcement of university regulations. This position is critical to maintaining continuous 24/7 campus security coverage, ensuring operational continuity and the university’s ability to respond effectively to emergencies without interruption. The Campus Security Officer exercises independent judgment and sound decision- making in alignment with established policies and procedures, ensuring appropriate escalation and communication, particularly during emergent and high-risk situations, and may be required to provide immediate response activities and coordination until emergency services arrive. The role supports the university, and is accountable for timely response, accurate reporting, and adherence to established procedures. This is a physically demanding role requiring work in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment, including the ability to work the required rotating shifts (days, nights, weekends, and holidays). SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES: Security Services Promote the safety and security of students, staff, visitors, and University property. Respond to, assess, and coordinate incidents and emergencies, including initial scene control, fact gathering, documentation, and reporting. Assist with other investigative activities as assigned Exercise independent judgment while escalating incidents in accordance with established protocols and maintaining communication with supervisors. Monitor and control access points; lock and unlock facilities based on operational schedules. Conduct proactive patrols, monitor facilities and access points, and ensure the physical security of campus property. Build positive relationships and provide assistance, information, and support to staff, students, and visitors. Serve as a operational contact for Casual Campus Security Officers, providing guidance, mentorship, and support. Collaborate with internal departments to support coordinated responses to safety, behavioral, and wellness concerns. Prepare clear, accurate, and thorough reports, and preserve evidence as required. Maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information in accordance with privacy legislation and university policies. Operate within the scope of authority defined by CBU Policies, other applicable legislation and Special Constable appointment, using appropriate and proportionate response measures. Administer First Aid/CPR and coordinate responses with emergency services (police, fire, EHS). Monitor and assist individuals in distress, ensuring appropriate intervention and escalation. Conduct traffic/parking enforcement. Conduct crowd and event coordination activities. Participate in fire safety programs, alarm testing, and emergency preparedness activities. On occasion, assist with conducting security audits and inspections, identifying risks and recommending corrective action Inspect safety equipment (e.g., fire extinguishers, AEDs) for operational readiness. Participate in the Safe Walk/Work Safe Program. Support operational continuity through consistent application of procedures and knowledge of campus-specific risks. Perform other related safety, security, and emergency coordination duties as assigned to support operational requirements. Education and Engagement Support and deliver safety education programs for students and staff, including: Personal safety and campus security Alcohol and drug awareness Sexual violence prevention and response Residence safety Emergency preparedness Promote awareness, engagement, and community trust through proactive outreach. QUALIFICATIONS AND SKILLS: Diploma or Certificate in policing, corrections, criminology, or equivalent experience. Minimum of 2 years’ experience in policing, corrections, or security services. Valid CPR, First Aid, and AED certification (or ability to obtain). Valid driver’s license with a clean abstract. Ability to obtain and maintain: Criminal Record Check Special Constable status (Applicable to Full-Time position only Core Competencies Demonstrated initiative and proactive approach to safety and security. Strong attention to detail, particularly in documentation and reporting. Effective interpersonal and communication skills, with strong de-escalation abilities. Comfortable using security-related technology to support daily operations, including CCTV and camera systems, access control systems, Microsoft 365, and electronic reporting and records management platforms. Physically capable of performing operational duties, including prolonged periods of activity and responding effectively to emergency situations. Proven ability to work in fast-paced, high-pressure environments and make sound decisions under stress. Experienced in shift work, including days, nights, weekends, and holidays in a fast-paced environment. Strong situational awareness and risk assessment skills. Professionalism, integrity, and confidentiality. Resilience and composure in stressful or potentially traumatic situations. Maintain all required certifications and competencies. Participate in ongoing training and professional development to support operational effectiveness. Willingness to complete additional training as required. Applications for the successful candidate will include a: cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant complete resume list of at least three references. Short listed candidates will be required to submit three reference letters. Please upload all required documents to Additional Documents if no designated area is listed . Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applications must be received by October 23, 2026 Select Apply above to start your application today! The union affiliation for this position is with the Nova Scotia Government & General Employees Union, Local 18, MOS. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/cbu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/1501": {
      "title": "Field Education Lead, BSW",
      "description": "Field Education Lead, BSW | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs CBU home English (United States) Sign In Field Education Lead, BSW Req #231 Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 5, 2026 at 7:00 PM | Expires Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 6:59 PM EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Please ensure you upload your resume, attach a cover letter,  list of references in the correct upload area. Any other documents required please add to Additional Documents. Cape Breton University (CBU) invites applications for a Full-Time Continuing, Field Education Lead in the Department of Social Work, School of Arts and Social Sciences . The successful candidate will provide leadership for the management, administration, educational quality, and community relationships that support field education within the BSW program. They will ensure that student practicums, field-related courses, policies, documentation, and evaluation processes align with CASWE accreditation standards, the CASWE Core Learning Objectives, institutional policies, and the mission and goals of the BSW program. Position Responsibilities: Reporting to and working with the Program Director, the Field Education Lead creates, facilitates, and assesses field practicum placements for social work students. Responsibilities include: Lead the management, administration, educational development, and evaluation of BSW field education, ensuring alignment with CASWE standards, Core Learning Objectives, institutional policies, and program outcomes. Maintain and oversee field education policies, procedures, documentation, learning contracts, evaluation processes, and related materials . Recruit, assess, approve, develop, support, and retain practicum agencies and qualified field supervisors , and assess placement capacity for Field Practicum I and II. Coordinate student placement processes , including meeting with students, assessing placement fit, managing placement decisions, and communicating with students, agencies, supervisors, and the Field Practice Educator. Support placement managers and field supervisors regarding practicum expectations, supervision, student learning, policies, documentation, and evaluation responsibilities . Ensure required student screening and placement documentation is completed and collaborate with the Field Practice Educator to address concerns related to student performance, conduct, attendance, supervision, safety, learning opportunities, or placement suitability. Build and maintain community partnerships with social workers and practicum settings and identify opportunities and trends to strengthen field education. Support professional development, research, collaborative initiatives, and university service related to the BSW program and community partnerships. Qualifications of this role are: Master of Social Work Degree (MSW); A minimum of five years of practice experience in the field of social work ; Understanding of social services, practice and placement requirements and standards , and current issues and trends in social work; Demonstrated commitment to the principles of social work education and practice , including, but not limited to, social justice, equity, diversity, inclusion, and decolonization; Understanding of social work education and practice in the context of rural, indigenous, and marginal communities at the micro, mezzo, and macro levels; Ability to work independently and as a team member , including the ability to develop interpersonal, collegial, and relationship-building skills suited to field education, social work education, university, and professional contexts; Flexibility with hours of work based on program operation needs (e.g., special events in the evening, early morning preparation for daytime special events, etc.); Ability to multitask priorities and responsibilities. Applications for the successful candidate will include: a cover letter describing the expertise of the applicant a complete resume (or CV) A list of least three references. All required documents must be uploaded to \"Additional Documents\" with correct titles for each required document. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, priority will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents. Applications must be received by 11:00PM on October 28th, 2026. Cape Breton University is strongly committed to fostering diversity within our community. We welcome those who would contribute to the further diversification of our staff, our faculty and its scholarship including, but not limited to, women, visible minorities, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and persons of any sexual orientation or gender identity. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply but applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. CBU is committed to Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (EDI) and applicants are encouraged to self-identity if they are part of a marginalised community, or have experience working with Indigenous communities. If we contact you for an interview and you are a person with a disability who requires technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Cape Breton University Human Resources Dept. HumanResouces@cbu.ca 1250 Grand Lake Road, Sydney, NS B1M 1A2 Scan this QR code and apply! Download Cape Breton University, 1250 Grand Lake Rd, Sydney, Nova Scotia, Canada ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Statement of Accessibility Cookie Preferences Delete Application Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    }
